There's no obvious way to implement the non-parametric analysis for a
2-QTL model;
the meaning of interaction is not clear when you're working with
ranks.  Thus,
I don't plan to implement such a thing for scantwo().

You might try converting the phenotypes to ranks and then just
plugging them into
scantwo() and seeing what happens.  Or you can convert ranks to
normal quantiles.

If your phenotype is y, you might use:

   y2 <- qnorm( (rank(y) - 0.5)/length(y) )

karl

