Thanks, Ani.

I would add to that: if you're looking at an intercross,
you'll want to convert the E4M8a data into two columns, one
for the additive effect and one for the dominance deviation,
as follows:

> markerdata <-pull.geno(mycross)
> E4M8a <- markerdata[,"E4M8a"]

addcov <- matrix(0, ncol=2, nrow=nind(mycross))
addcov[E4M8a==1,1] <- -1
addcov[E4M8a==3,1] <- 1
addcov[E4M8a==2,2] <- 1

